          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is a mile on a treadmill the same as a mile outside?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "In distance, yes, allowing for console accuracy. In effort, walking is close to identical, and running on a belt is commonly held to be slightly easier than the road because there is no air resistance and the surface is perfectly even. Setting a 1% incline to compensate is a widely used convention rather than a measured correction.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      description: description,
      author: { "@type": "Person", name: "Morgan Reyes" },
      datePublished: "2026-10-08",
      dateModified: "2026-10-08",
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" },
